, so adding them all gives the value.","20":"Return the value of the expression."},"py":{"3":"<code>terms</code> holds the signed values that get added at the end; products and quotients are folded in.","4":"<code>num</code> builds the current number; <code>op</code> is the operator waiting in front of it.","5":"The extra <code>+</code> at the end forces the pending operator to apply to the last number.","6":"Spaces carry no meaning.","7":"Skip the space and read the next character.","8":"A digit extends the number being read.","9":"Shift the number one decimal place and add this digit.","10":"The number may have more digits, so keep reading.","11":"A pending <code>+</code> starts a new positive term.","12":"Push the number as its own term.","13":"A pending <code>-</code> starts a new negative term.","14":"Push the negated number as its own term.","15":"Multiplication binds tighter than addition, so it changes the last term.","16":"Fold <code>num</code> into the last term instead of starting a new one.","18":"Division binds tighter too: take the last term out to divide it.","19":"Divide the size only, since Python's <code>//</code> rounds negatives down, not toward zero.","20":"Put the sign back and store the truncated quotient as the last term.","21":"This operator now waits for the next number, which starts from zero.","22":"Every term is final, so their sum is the value of the expression."}}},{"ts":{"steps":[{"l":2,"d":0,"fn":"calculate","v":{"s":" 2+3*4 - 6/4","total":0},"stack":[],"ch":["total"]},{"l":2,"d":0,"fn":"calculate","v":{"term":0},"ch":["term"]},{"l":2,"d":0,"fn":"calculate","v":{"num":0},"ch":["num"]},{"l":2,"d":0,"fn":"calculate","v":{"op":"+"},"ch":["op"]},{"l":3,"d":0,"fn":"calculate","v":{"i":0},"ch":["i"]},{"l":4,"d":0,"fn":"calculate","v":{"c":" "},"ch":["c"]},{"l":5,"d":0,"fn":"calculate","v":{}},{"l":5,"d":0,"fn":"calculate","v":{},"x":["c"]},{"l":3,"d":0,"fn":"calculate","v":{"i":1},"ch":["i"]},{"l":4,"d":0,"fn":"calculate","v":{"c":"2"},"ch